  "verbalization": "Cortisone is linked to SW1353 through Granzyme B, which is targeted by both Isolicarin A and (1R,4Z,6R,7S,11R,17S)-4-ethylidene-7-hydroxy-6,7-dimethyl-2,9-dioxa-14-azatricyclo[9.5.1.014,17]heptadecane-3,8-dione. This suggests that cortisone may act as a modulator of Granzyme B activity, potentially influencing its interaction with SW1353. The presence of multiple targets for Granzyme B, including both natural compounds and cortisone, indicates a possible regulatory role of cortisone in the biological process that leads to SW1353 activation. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, where cortisone could either directly or indirectly influence the target of Granzyme B, thereby affecting SW1353. The evidence supports a mechanism where cortisone may serve as a signaling molecule that modulates Granzyme B activity, which in turn affects SW1353.",
